abstract: |
  A unified theoretical framework consisting of five foundational papers: 
  (1) Adaptive Resistance and Impedance Networks (ARP/AIN),
  (2) Adaptive-π Geometry and Calculus,
  (3) Curve Memory and Curve Memory Alphabet (CM/CMA),
  (4) Phase-Lift, PR-Root, and Phase-Resistant Objects (PROs),
  (5) QPS-GR Strain, Clock Offset, Visibility, and Refresh Mapping. 
  
  This work establishes canonical notation and semantics for adaptive
  geometric systems with memory, phase-structured branching, and quantum-GR
  correspondence layers.